course: dictionary
lesson: 2917
title: Drain: one word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and context tells you which one fits. The word drain can be a verb (to drain something) or a noun (a drain). «Drain the pasta» means pour the water out, so drain is about liquid flowing out of something.
explain: «Using someone's phone without asking can drain their battery when they need it.» Nothing is flowing out of the phone, so ask what the sentence means. The battery is being used up slowly. Swap in "use up slowly": "Using someone's phone can use up their battery." It still makes sense, so drain means use up slowly here.
explain: Drain is also a noun: a drain is a pipe or hole that takes dirty water or rainwater away. «Deep or flooded puddles can hide holes, drains and sharp things.» Here drains are things you could not see under the water. Feeling drained is different again: it means feeling very tired.
fact: Drain can be a verb (drain, drains, drained, draining) or a noun (a drain, drains).
fact: To drain is to let water or another liquid flow out of something, as in «drain the pasta».
fact: A drain is a pipe or hole that takes dirty water or rainwater away.
fact: To drain something is to use it up slowly, as in «the game drained my phone battery».
fact: «Down the drain» means wasted, so time or money spent for nothing has gone down the drain.
exercise: «Drain the pasta before you serve it.» What does drain mean here? | *Let the water flow out | A pipe that takes rainwater away | Use up slowly | Feel very tired
exercise: «Never play near storm drains, the water can be fast and deep.» What is a storm drain? | A rainy-day jacket | *A pipe or hole that carries rainwater away | A puddle that never dries | A fast, deep river
exercise: To feel drained means to feel | Cold and wet | *Very tired | Full of energy | Very happy
test: «The game drained my phone battery.» What does drained mean? | Let water flow out | Cleaned | *Used up slowly | Lost in the rain
test: What does «down the drain» mean? | Full of water | *Wasted | Found again | Hidden under the floor
exam: Which meaning of drain fits «Using someone's phone without asking can drain their battery when they need it»? | A pipe or hole that takes water away | To let water flow out | To feel very tired | *To use up slowly
